    <!-- Device log (live syslog off the iPhone) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Title">Device log</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Hint">Live log from the iPhone itself. Use it when an app installs but will not open: the reason is reported by the device and appears nowhere in the application log.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Open">Open device log</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.OpenHint">Start the capture, then reproduce the problem on the phone — install the app and tap its icon. Save the log afterwards and send it over.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Start">Start capture</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Stop">Stop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Save">Save to file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FilterInstall">Install and launch only</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.AutoScroll">Follow new lines</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Streaming">Capturing…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Stopped">Stopped</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Idle">Ready</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.NoDevice">No device connected</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Saved">Log saved</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.SaveFailed">Could not save the log</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FilterChanged">The filter applies to new lines; lines already collected are unchanged.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Hint.Reproduce">Now reproduce the problem on the phone: install the app and tap its icon.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.Footer">Red lines name a failure outright. Save the file and send it over if the cause is not obvious.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.Title">The device rejected the app's FairPlay licence</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.Detail">This is why the app shows a white screen and closes: it installed correctly, but the device cannot decrypt it. Open the App Store on the phone, sign in with the same Apple ID the app was downloaded with, and start downloading any free app — beginning the download is enough, it need not finish. Then try the installed app again.</sys:String>
    <!-- {0} is the Apple ID. Accounts match, so the licence just has not been issued yet. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.SameAccount">The app installed correctly but the device cannot decrypt it. The Apple ID matches ({0}), so the account is not the problem: the phone has not yet been issued a licence by the App Store. Open the App Store on the phone, confirm it is signed in as {0}, and start downloading any free app — beginning the download is enough, it need not finish. Then try the installed app again.</sys:String>
    <!-- Recovery kept being retried and kept failing, so waiting is not the answer. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.RecoveryRefused">The phone has now asked the App Store for this app's licence several times over and been refused every time — waiting longer, or opening the App Store, will not change that. A FairPlay licence belongs to the account the file was downloaded under, and the phone can only ask for one for the account it is signed in to. The way out is to download this app here under the account the phone is signed in to, then install it again.</sys:String>
    <!-- {0} is the Apple ID on the phone. Same as above, but able to name the account. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.RecoveryRefusedFor">The phone has asked the App Store for this app's licence several times over — as {0} — and been refused every time. That means {0} does not own this app: the licence belongs to whichever account the file was downloaded under. Waiting and opening the App Store will not help. Download this app here under {0} and install it again, or sign the phone in as the account that owns the licence.</sys:String>
    <!-- The phone asked for the licence itself, so the manual App Store trip is unnecessary. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.Recovering">The app installed correctly, but the phone had no licence for it yet at that first launch. There is no need to open the App Store: the device has already requested one by itself — the log shows "fairplay recovery". Wait 10-20 seconds with the phone online, then tap the app on the home screen again. If it is still a white screen after two or three tries the request did not get through, and that is when starting any free App Store download helps.</sys:String>
    <!-- {0} is the download account, {1} the account on the phone. Nothing on the phone fixes this. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.DeviceLogs.FairPlay.OtherAccount">The app was downloaded under Apple ID {0}, but the phone is signed in as {1}. A FairPlay licence is issued to one account, so this copy will not launch on this phone whatever you do in the App Store. Either sign the phone in as {0}, or download the app again here under {1} and reinstall it.</sys:String>

