    <!-- Throughput advisor -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Tuning.Defender.Title">Defender is scanning the download folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Tuning.Defender.Detail">Every block written into the IPA is checked by the antivirus, and the finished archive is scanned again in full. On multi-gigabyte files this is usually the largest loss of speed. Adding the folder to the exclusion list requires administrator rights.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Tuning.CrossVolume.Title">Temporary folder is on a different drive</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Tuning.CrossVolume.Detail">Staging is on {0} while the destination folder is on {1}. The final move becomes a full copy of the archive instead of an instant rename.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Tuning.Compressed.Title">The download folder is NTFS-compressed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Tuning.Compressed.Detail">An IPA is already compressed, so NTFS compression saves no space but turns sequential writes into read-modify-write cycles.</sys:String>
